  "nl_text": "The database schema for the database named rschema_0193 consists of five tables: 'material', 'project', 'material_usage_record', 'department', and 'employee'.\nThe 'material' table represents the materials that are used in the projects. It has five columns: 'material_id', 'material_name', 'specifications', 'unit_price', and 'inventory'. 'material_id' is the primary key of this table.\nThe 'project' table represents the projects. It has seven columns: 'project_id', 'project_name', 'start_date', 'expected_completion_date', 'actual_completion_date', 'project_budget', and 'project_location'. 'project_id' is the primary key of this table.\nThe 'material_usage_record' table represents the usage records of the materials in the projects. It has six columns: 'usage_record_id', 'project_id', 'material_id', 'usage_date', 'usage_quantity', and 'usage_employee_id'. 'usage_record_id' is the primary key of this table. 'employee_id', 'material_id', and 'project_id' are foreign keys referencing 'employee', 'material', and 'project' respectively.\nThe 'department' table represents the departments. It has two columns: 'department_id' and 'department_name'. 'department_id' is the primary key of this table.\nThe 'employee' table represents the employees. It has three columns: 'employee_id', 'employee_name', and 'department_id'. 'employee_id' is the primary key of this table. 'department_id' is a foreign key referencing 'department' and has ON DELETE CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE options.\nThis schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing foreign key constraints. When a record in the 'employee', 'material', or 'project' table is deleted or updated, the corresponding records in the 'material_usage_record' table will also be deleted or updated to maintain the consistency of the data.",
  "gold_question": "A construction and installation company is responsible for the supply of materials for multiple projects. Each material has a material number, name, specification, unit price and inventory. Each project needs to record the materials used and their quantity, date of use, department using them and employee using them. The material management information system needs to be able to count the use of materials and manage inventory.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0193.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0193\nCREATE TABLE `material` (\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `specifications` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `inventory` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`material_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `expected_completion_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `actual_completion_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_budget` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `material_usage_record` (\n  `usage_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `usage_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`usage_record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `material_usage_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `material_usage_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`material_id`) REFERENCES `material` (`material_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `material_usage_record_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`usage_employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
